--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/COURSE_AGGREGATE_ENDPOINT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,147 @@
+# GET /courses/:id — Aggregated Course Page Response
+
+## Summary
+
+`GET /courses/:id` now returns everything the Course page needs in a single
+response: the course, its videos, the authenticated user's enrollment (if
+any), and that user's video-progress records (scoped to this course).
+
+Frontend no longer needs to separately call enrollment-status or per-video
+progress endpoints when initializing the Course page.
+
+- **Route:** unchanged — still `GET /courses/:id`
+- **Auth:** unchanged — `authenticateToken` only (same as before; course
+  viewing has never been enrollment-gated, only video streaming is)
+- **Envelope:** unchanged — `{ success, data }` / `{ success: false, error }`
+- **Excluded:** quizzes, assignments, and any other unrelated resource
+
+## Authentication
+
+**Required.** Send the access token via the `accessToken`/`token` cookie or
+an `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header, per existing auth conventions.
+
+## Request
+
+```
+GET /courses/:id
+```
+
+| Param | Type   | Description        |
+|-------|--------|---------------------|
+| `id`  | number | Course ID (path)   |
+
+## Response — 200 OK
+
+```json
+{
+  "success": true,
+  "data": {
+    "course": {
+      "id": 1,
+      "title": "Introduction to JavaScript",
+      "description": "Learn the basics of JavaScript programming",
+      "price": 49.99,
+      "thumbnail": "https://api.example.com/uploads/thumbnails/js-intro.jpg",
+      "isYoutube": false,
+      "youtubePlaylistId": null,
+      "teacherId": 4,
+      "teacher": { "id": 4, "name": "Mona Youssef", "email": "mona@example.com" },
+      "createdAt": "2023-01-15T12:00:00.000Z",
+      "category": "Programming",
+      "grade": "THIRD_SECONDARY"
+    },
+    "videos": [
+      {
+        "id": 10,
+        "title": "Variables and Data Types",
+        "url": "https://api.example.com/uploads/videos/v1.mp4",
+        "thumbnail": "https://api.example.com/uploads/thumbnails/v1.jpg",
+        "duration": 1200,
+        "position": 1
+      },
+      {
+        "id": 11,
+        "title": "Functions and Scope",
+        "url": "https://api.example.com/uploads/videos/v2.mp4",
+        "thumbnail": "https://api.example.com/uploads/thumbnails/v2.jpg",
+        "duration": 1500,
+        "position": 2
+      }
+    ],
+    "enrollment": {
+      "id": 77,
+      "userId": 42,
+      "courseId": 1,
+      "isPaid": true,
+      "paymentDate": "2023-02-01T09:00:00.000Z",
+      "progress": 50,
+      "startedAt": "2023-02-01T09:00:00.000Z",
+      "completedAt": null,
+      "isCompleted": false,
+      "lastAccess": "2023-06-10T18:22:00.000Z",
+      "createdAt": "2023-02-01T09:00:00.000Z"
+    },
+    "progress": [
+      { "videoId": 10, "completed": true, "watchedAt": "2023-06-01T10:00:00.000Z" },
+      { "videoId": 11, "completed": false, "watchedAt": null }
+    ]
+  }
+}
+```
+
+### Field notes
+
+- **`course`** — same fields as before, minus the `videos` and `enrollments`
+  arrays that used to be nested inside it (those are now their own top-level
+  keys below).
+- **`videos`** — the course's videos, ordered by `position` ascending (same
+  field/convention already used by `nextVideoController` and
+  `sequentialAccess`). `url`/`thumbnail` are absolutized the same way as
+  before.
+- **`enrollment`** — the **authenticated user's own** enrollment row for this
+  course, or `null` if they aren't enrolled. Resolved from the JWT (`req.user.id`)
+  only — never from a client-supplied user ID.
+  - ⚠️ **Behavior change:** previously this endpoint returned an array of
+    *every* user's enrollment (`id`, `userId`, `createdAt`) for the course to
+    anyone who could view the course. That was a data leak and has been
+    fixed — `enrollment` is now a single object (or `null`), scoped to the
+    caller.
+- **`progress`** — one entry per video in the course, for the authenticated
+  user only. A video the user hasn't started has no `VideoProgress` row, so
+  it's represented as `{ completed: false, watchedAt: null }` — the same
+  "empty" shape already used by `videoProgressController`'s
+  `checkVideoCompletion`/`getCourseVideoProgress`, not a new convention.
+
+## Error responses
+
+Unchanged from before:
+
+| Status | Condition                                  |
+|--------|---------------------------------------------|
+| 401    | No/invalid/expired token                    |
+| 404    | `{ "success": false, "error": "Course not found" }` |
+| 500    | `{ "success": false, "error": "Failed to fetch course" }` |
+
+Non-enrolled users are **not** blocked from viewing a course (no change here)
+— they simply get `enrollment: null` and `progress` entries all showing
+`completed: false`.
+
+## Migrating existing frontend code
+
+Old pattern (multiple requests):
+
+```
+GET /courses/:id                 → course (with nested videos + all enrollments)
+GET /enroll/status (body: {courseId}) → this user's enrollment
+GET /video-progress/course/:courseId  → this user's progress
+```
+
+New pattern (one request):
+
+```
+GET /courses/:id → { course, videos, enrollment, progress }
+```
+
+The standalone `/enroll/*` and `/video-progress/*` endpoints still exist and
+work as before (untouched) — the Course page just doesn't need to call them
+separately anymore for initial load.
-- 
